    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1489">

                <pb facs="1293" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/237</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 7, 7 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1989. Department’s 1423. Foreign Office replies that military authorities unaware
                    of any attack on <hi rendition="#italic">Elfland</hi> on 21st. If any mistake
                        <pb facs="1294" n="1036" xml:id="pg1036"/> in identity were made it must be
                    ascribed to exceptional difficulty of work of submarines and aeroplanes. They
                    are minutely informed regarding markings and movements of commission’s ships.
                    Government recommends that horizontal markings on deck of ships be erected. Copy
                    note mailed Hague and commission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
